@UserManagementAPI_HostAddress = http://localhost:5070
# Development token from appsettings.Development.json. That file is git-ignored (see the repo .gitignore),
# so on a fresh clone set a token first, e.g.:
#   dotnet user-secrets set "Authentication:Clients:0:Name" "local-dev"
#   dotnet user-secrets set "Authentication:Clients:0:Token" "dev-only-token-change-me-0123456789"
@token = dev-only-token-change-me-0123456789

### ---------- Happy path ----------

### Get users (paged; total count in the X-Total-Count header)
GET {{UserManagementAPI_HostAddress}}/api/users?page=1&pageSize=50
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Accept: application/json

### Create a user -> 201 Created (fields are trimmed, email lower-cased)
POST {{UserManagementAPI_HostAddress}}/api/users
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "Avery",
  "lastName": "Morgan",
  "email": "avery.morgan@techhive.example",
  "department": "Engineering"
}

### Get a user by ID -> 200
GET {{UserManagementAPI_HostAddress}}/api/users/1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Accept: application/json

### Update a user -> 200
PUT {{UserManagementAPI_HostAddress}}/api/users/1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "Avery",
  "lastName": "Morgan",
  "email": "avery.morgan@techhive.example",
  "department": "Platform Engineering"
}

### Delete a user -> 204
DELETE {{UserManagementAPI_HostAddress}}/api/users/1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### ---------- Edge cases ----------

### Invalid input -> 400 with an error per field
POST {{UserManagementAPI_HostAddress}}/api/users
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "",
  "lastName": "M0rgan",
  "email": "a@b",
  "department": "X"
}

### Malformed JSON -> 400 (not 500)
POST {{UserManagementAPI_HostAddress}}/api/users
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ oops

### Duplicate email (case-insensitive) -> 409 Conflict (run "Create a user" first)
POST {{UserManagementAPI_HostAddress}}/api/users
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "Blake",
  "lastName": "Lee",
  "email": "AVERY.MORGAN@techhive.example",
  "department": "Sales"
}

### Non-existent user -> 404 ProblemDetails
GET {{UserManagementAPI_HostAddress}}/api/users/999
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Non-numeric ID -> 404 ProblemDetails
GET {{UserManagementAPI_HostAddress}}/api/users/abc
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Update a non-existent user -> 404
PUT {{UserManagementAPI_HostAddress}}/api/users/999
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "Avery",
  "lastName": "Morgan",
  "email": "someone@techhive.example",
  "department": "Engineering"
}

### Delete a non-existent user -> 404
DELETE {{UserManagementAPI_HostAddress}}/api/users/999
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Invalid paging -> 400
GET {{UserManagementAPI_HostAddress}}/api/users?page=0&pageSize=500
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### ---------- Authentication / middleware ----------

### No token -> 401 Unauthorized
GET {{UserManagementAPI_HostAddress}}/api/users

### Invalid token -> 401 Unauthorized (WWW-Authenticate: Bearer error="invalid_token")
GET {{UserManagementAPI_HostAddress}}/api/users
Authorization: Bearer not-a-real-token-0123456789

### Wrong scheme -> 401 Unauthorized
GET {{UserManagementAPI_HostAddress}}/api/users
Authorization: Basic dXNlcjpwYXNz

### OpenAPI document is allowed without a token in Development
GET {{UserManagementAPI_HostAddress}}/openapi/v1.json
